e to make <i>petrificatus</i> generation more likely despite Disquiet, and somehow convince the local graveyards to look the other way despite Disquiet, and have somehow acquired the infrastructure to reliably contain their ballooning Automaton population, and somehow identify Alchemists/Sublimati/Centimani that won't immediately harvest and/or eat them, and somehow convince them that the long-term gains are worth more than harvesting/eating them right now, and somehow managing to keep all this from self destructing because of Disquiet. The returns are still not going to be worth the effort. It requires new bodies constantly, I highly doubt destroyed <i>petrificatus</i> can be recycled given their propensity for dissolving, and every new body is only 1 more Vitriol. The myriad uses Vitriol has for Alchemists especially makes a constant supply extremely attractive. This is tailor-made to turn &amp;quot;reasonable&amp;quot; Alchemists into insatiable ones. Sublimati are irrational at the best of times and still need to eat Prometheans [or people] for Pyros. Plus they get pretty limited benefits from Vitriol, most of which come down to &amp;quot;the better to eat you with&amp;quot;.<br /> As Gizmit said, Centimani are probably the only group that you can hope to forge any kind of lasting peace with such a farm, and their thoughts and personality are constantly eroding under Flux's influence. I would not put much trust in them honoring any agreements they have made in the past. But, any Promethean participating is likely either already a Centimanus, on the fast track to becoming one, or stuck in a particularly cruel Role [and ironically, potentially at risk of becoming the very thing they're helping to farm], so who knows?<br /> <br /> Basically, it is a ridiculous amount of work, requires extraordinarily intimate knowledge of the <i>petrificatus</i> condition, enough political power to get authorities to the look the other way, and at a certain point, it becomes easier to hunt and harvest Prometheans. So, while, technically, yes it can happen, the actual process is so contrived as to be basically impossible, requires a pet mage, will not realistically yield enough returns to be worth it, will collapse under its own weight eventually, and is <i>very clearly</i> not intended by the rules.<br /> But if it works for your game and you're excited about the possibility, well, we can't stop you.<br /> <br /> All of this said, it could be very cool to confront players with a ghost town full of <i>petrificati</i> leftover from a failed farming attempt. It could be almost like a zombie movie, but the real danger comes from all the Pandorans surely lying dormant nearby.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's see, an elaborate stage to contain the roles, lots of use of the Disquietism Transmutation, Alembics or Athanors that help transfer pyros so cannibalism can be avoided, routes and schedules that avoid wasteland and Disquiet build-up, dire leverage probably obtained by Cathars, hiring the Stormbringer and the Golden Friends.<br /> <br /> The more I think about it the more elaborate the program needs to be. You may not think it is worth it, but it can separate Vitriol from Lacunae. That alone is worth a billion dollars. <br /> <br /> Alternatively, we could have a Promethean near the end of the Pilgrimage create Vitriol Fount after Vitriol Fount, his resources constantly replenished from his success according to the rules and make this a tradition among Primetheans. That would take decades though, so I like my other idea better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-18T04:27:22-08:00","id":1424681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1421125-farming-vitriol?p=1424675#post1424675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let's see, an elaborate stage to contain the roles, lots of use of the Disquietism Transmutation, Alembics or Athanors that help transfer pyros so cannibalism can be avoided, routes and schedules that avoid wasteland and Disquiet build-up, dire leverage probably obtained by Cathars, hiring the Stormbringer and the Golden Friends.<br /> <br /> The more I think about it the more elaborate the program needs to be. You may not think it is worth it, but it can separate Vitriol from Lacunae. That alone is worth a billion dollars. <br /> <br /> Alternatively, we could have a Promethean near the end of the Pilgrimage create Vitriol Fount after Vitriol Fount, his resources constantly replenished from his success according to the rules and make this a tradition among Primetheans. That would take decades though, so I like my other idea better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems a lot of complications.<br /> If you search easy vitriol there it is an easier way.<br /> One promethean in the graveyard, performs the generative act on all the incoming corpses.<br /> His percentage of success would be a lot better than a Petrificatus.<br /> Cage all the resulting prometheans until they starts the pilgrimage.<br /> Kill them and wait for the automatic reanimation.<br /> Perform lacuna to harvest the vitriol resulting from this Universal milestone, than kill them again.<br /> Put the corpses back in the tombs.<br /> Easier and cleaner.<br /> <br /> The only point i don t understand is, do you think that promethean on pilgrimage can use your method because harvesting vitriol from Petrificatus is not considerred a Lacuna? If yes why?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T17:51:07-08:00","id":1427231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1421125-farming-vitriol?p=1424681#post1424681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seems a lot of complications.<br /> If you search easy vitriol there it is an easier way.<br /> One promethean in the graveyard, performs the generative act on all the incoming corpses.<br /> His percentage of success would be a lot better than a Petrificatus.<br /> Cage all the resulting prometheans until they starts the pilgrimage.<br /> Kill them and wait for the automatic reanimation.<br /> Perform lacuna to harvest the vitriol resulting from this Universal milestone, than kill them again.<br /> Put the corpses back in the tombs.<br /> Easier and cleaner.<br /> <br /> The only point i don t understand is, do you think that promethean on pilgrimage can use your method because harvesting vitriol from Petrificatus is not considerred a Lacuna? If yes why?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> you thoroughly missed the point of it all. This is not about Prometheans on the Pilgrimage. They will make their own Vitriol and that is enough. This is about freeing them from predation and Lacunae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T23:46:08-08:00","id":1427250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1421125-farming-vitriol?p=1427231#post1427231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> you thoroughly missed the point of it all. This is not about Prometheans on the Pilgrimage. They will make their own Vitriol and that is enough. This is about freeing them from predation and Lacunae.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that s the point... now i can see it working.<br /> I could really enjoy a group or alchemist/centimanus approaching a pc throng on the pilgrimage and say &quot;we ll spare your life IF you give us a continuous stream of cash to finance our little project&quot;.<br /> A good ethical dilemma.<br /> From an organizative viewpoint i would keep things simplier, less variables means less resources needed and less things that could go wrong.<br /> I think that a buisness oriented conspirancy would prefer a method like that of my previous example, as it would give more results with less work, but i can see that your point is to create a really horrific situation.<br /> Overall it could be a good plot hook","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T04:21:16-08:00","id":1429129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1421125-farming-vitriol?p=1427250#post1427250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If that s the point... now i can see it working.<br /> I could really enjoy a group or alchemist/centimanus approaching a pc throng on the pilgrimage and say &quot;we ll spare your life IF you give us a continuous stream of cash to finance our little project&quot;.<br /> A good ethical dilemma.<br /> From an organizative viewpoint i would keep things simplier, less variables means less resources needed and less things that could go wrong.<br /> I think that a buisness oriented conspirancy would prefer a method like that of my previous example, as it would give more results with less work, but i can see that your point is to create a really horrific situation.<br /> Overall it could be a good plot hook</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My point &quot;is&quot; to create a horrific situation or my point is that it &quot;would&quot; make a horrific situation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T11:31:45-08:00","id":1429198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1421125-farming-vitriol?p=1429129#post1429129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> My point &amp;quot;is&amp;quot; to create a horrific situation or my point is that it &amp;quot;would&amp;quot; make a horrific situation?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, if you are GMing for a group of players with in pilgrimage promethean characters, and you presents this scenario runned by centimanus, alchemists and sublimatus, the players could feel disturbed in an entertaining way","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-23T03:31:15-08:00","id":1429603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1421125-farming-vitriol?p=1429198#post1429198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, if you are GMing for a group of players with in pilgrimage promethean characters, and you presents this scenario runned by centimanus, alchemists and sublimatus, the players could feel disturbed in an entertaining way</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> oh, grammer can be confusing. How would one foster trust from Pilgrimage abiding Prometheans?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-23T04:11:25-08:00","id":1429607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1421125-farming-vitriol?p=1429603#post1429603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> oh, grammer can be confusing. How would one foster trust from Pilgrimage abiding Prometheans?</div> </div> </div> </div>Now that i think about it, this project would work very well with the criminal funerary business.<br /> I don t know if you are familiar with it, in some countries, expecially in south italy, local organized crime families coerce people to buy funerary services only from companies controlled by those criminal groups, who gain a percentage of the profits.<br /> Their methods consists on veiled threats, bribes and in extreme cases murder of beloved ones.<br /> <br /> Considering the level of organization that this project requires, i think that it could appear and work similary to those criminal group.<br /> They would not see a Pilgrimage promethean as a source of pyros or vitriol, but as a potential recruit and they would try to buy their loyalty with bribes.<br /> If bribes fails, then they would use threats to ensure that nobody reveals the nature of the project to cops, and they would surely have some corrupted cops on their payroll.<br /> Also, some Centimanus could also use Flux powers to turn local citizens against an enemy Promethean.<br /> <br /> Players would be put against a dilemma, stay silent or even join them in exchange of security and resources, or oppose them at great risks and little gain","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-28T01:13:10-08:00","id":1433688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1421125-farming-vitriol?p=1429607#post1429607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now that i think about it, this project would work very well with the criminal funerary business.<br /> I don t know if you are familiar with it, in some countries, expecially in south italy, local organized crime families coerce people to buy funerary services only from companies controlled by those criminal groups, who gain a percentage of the profits.<br /> Their methods consists on veiled threats, bribes and in extreme cases murder of beloved ones.<br /> <br /> Considering the level of organization that this project requires, i think that it could appear and work similary to those criminal group.<br /> They would not see a Pilgrimage promethean as a source of pyros or vitriol, but as a potential recruit and they would try to buy their loyalty with bribes.<br /> If bribes fails, then they would use threats to ensure that nobody reveals the nature of the project to cops, and they would surely have some corrupted cops on their payroll.<br /> Also, some Centimanus could also use Flux powers to turn local citizens against an enemy Promethean.<br /> <br /> Players would be put against a dilemma, stay silent or even join them in exchange of security and resources, or oppose them at great risks and little gain</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> yeesh. what a harsh world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-29T23:11:01-08:00","id":1433888,"title":"","content":"Wait, why are people saying you need a Fate mage, or sublimati and centimani and so forth?<br /> Anyway, I love these guys both for their humane (100% certified mindless beings) vitriol manufacturing and for how you can have a whole town of apparently normal looking folks who are completely mindless (this says a lot about society). Great ST possibilities.<br /> Perhaps the most important part, however, is a reason for pandorans to show up that isn't insanely infrequent.<br /> I am sad that the tormented stuff was cut. Although I'm not sure what the point of P-zombies experiencing torment is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-30T00:59:35-08:00","id":1433892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1421125-farming-vitriol?p=1433888#post1433888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, why are people saying you need a Fate mage, or sublimati and centimani and so forth?</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the small success ratio of the &quot;generative act&quot; performed by Petrificati a fate mage could increase the odds.<br /> Sublimati or centimani would probably be the starters of the project, as they benefit the most by vitriol harvest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-27T00:07:36-08:00","id":1437206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1421125-farming-vitriol?p=1433892#post1433892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Considering the small success ratio of the &amp;quot;generative act&amp;quot; performed by Petrificati a fate mage could increase the odds.<br /> Sublimati or centimani would probably be the starters of the project, as they benefit the most by vitriol harvest.</div> </div> </div> </div>The whole purpose is to bribe them into not eating Prometheans. Given that Lacunae are breaking points on the Pilgrimage and Prometheans can make their own Vitriol, it was never intended for Prometheans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-28T17:37:18-08:00","id":1437409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1421125-farming-vitriol?p=1433888#post1433888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am sad that the tormented stuff was cut. Although I'm not sure what the point of P-zombies experiencing torment is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two reasons. The first was philosophical: if the P-Zombies can feel anguish and anger, they aren't really P-Zombies. They have enough of a mind to experience terrible feelings, but just aren't detectable to empaths and telepaths. That means Torment is an actual condition imposed by the Divine Fire, and not just a game system to show the misery of the Promethean condition. That comes with a load of things for the PCs to think about their own existence.<br /> <br /> The second reason was that Tormented beings are likely to lash out, creating more bodies, and thus more chances for the Stuck to reproduce. It also means that Petrificati CAN change, if only for the worst. Gives a dangling thread for players that want to rekindle a Petrificatus's Azoth.<br /> My players, sadly, quickly assumed there was no way to fix the Stuck. They put Good Cop/Bad Cop down, and then went after the Centimanus in the hills. I never wrote rules for Petrificati redemption nor made any sort of decision on if it was possible as the campaign wrapped up a few sessions later. So it's up to individual Storytellers to decide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23990-gizmit","name":"Gizmit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23990_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}